@page "/table/{Id}"

@*
    ⚠️ The render mode is named here and nowhere else. The page around it is static SSR, which
    is the default and the thing that cannot be walked back cheaply (§3.11 C12). Your seat and
    the hand are inside this island, not a second one.

    🔥 There is no lede (BUILD-PLAN P13.5). The three sentences that used to open this page said
    what the table is and how concealment works; they are in AboutTable, one press away, and in
    the rules page. A table is a place, and a place does not introduce itself.

    ⚠️ Which table and who you are cross the render-mode boundary, so both are strings
    (BUILD-PLAN P13.6). A parameter handed to an interactive root component is serialised to
    the circuit; a HostedTable is not serialisable and must not be — the island looks it up in
    the lobby it is injected with, which is also what keeps every table in the site reachable
    only through the lobby.
*@
<PageTitle>Burmese Poker — the table</PageTitle>

<TableView @rendermode="InteractiveServer" TableId="@Id" You="@You" />

@code {
    /// <summary>Which table this URL names.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string Id { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>
    /// What to call you, from the lobby's own form. Absent means you came to watch.
    /// </summary>
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "you")]
    public string? You { get; set; }
}
